Subject: [PATCH 25/29] PS2: flush batched draws before changing the viewport

Batched triangles derive their scissor rectangle from the viewport at
flush time, so a viewport change must flush the pending batch first.
Without this, triangles queued under one viewport can be drawn with the
scissor of the next one, which shows up as horizontal streaks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019yH2brr5GjCGyCE62bYyXR
---
 src/graphics/PS2GS.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/graphics/PS2GS.cpp b/src/graphics/PS2GS.cpp
index e89da03..d3188f5 100644
--- a/src/graphics/PS2GS.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/PS2GS.cpp
@@ -273,6 +273,9 @@ void PS2GS::GetViewport(ZunViewport &out)
 
 void PS2GS::SetViewport(const ZunViewport &vp)
 {
+    /* Batched triangles derive their scissor from the viewport at flush time,
+       so flush them under the viewport they were submitted with. */
+    FlushPending();
     viewport = vp;
 }
 
